    <!-- 3. INFORMATION WE COLLECT -->
    <section id="information-we-collect">
      <h2>3. Information We Collect</h2>

      <h3>3.1 Information you provide</h3>
      <p>
        SafeHSE is designed to work offline and does <strong>not</strong> require
        you to create an account, log in, or provide personal information to use
        its core features.
      </p>
      <p>We do <strong>not</strong> collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name, phone number, or email address (unless you contact us voluntarily by email)</li>
        <li>Your precise location</li>
        <li>Your contacts</li>
        <li>Your photos or files</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>3.2 Information stored locally on your device</h3>
      <p>
        To provide its functionality, SafeHSE saves the following information
        <strong>only on your device</strong> using your device's local storage
        (AsyncStorage). This data is <strong>never transmitted to us</strong>:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your selected language preference</li>
        <li>Chapters you have marked as completed</li>
        <li>Bookmarks you have saved</li>
        <li>Personal notes you have written</li>
        <li>Mock test results and scores</li>
        <li>Incorrect questions you want to review</li>
        <li>Your daily learning streak</li>
        <li>Notification preferences</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can delete this data at any time from
        <strong>Settings → Reset All Progress</strong>, or by uninstalling the App.
      </p>

      <h3>3.3 Information collected automatically by us</h3>
      <p>
        Aside from the advertising SDK described in Section 4, SafeHSE does
        <strong>not</strong> use analytics, crash reporters, or tracking
        libraries. We do not maintain servers that collect usage statistics,
        device information, or IP addresses.
      </p>

      <h3>3.4 Information collected by Google Play</h3>
      <p>
        If you install the App through Google Play, Google may collect basic
        installation and crash data as part of its standard Play Store services.
        This is governed by
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's own privacy policy</a>,
        not ours.
      </p>

      <h3>3.5 Notifications</h3>
      <p>
        If you enable study reminders, the App uses your device's local
        notification system (Expo Notifications). We do not store the content of
        notifications on any server. You can disable notifications at any time
        from your device settings or from within the App.
      </p>

      <h3>3.6 Email correspondence</h3>
      <p>
        If you contact us by email at
        <a href="mailto:[your-email@example.com]">[your-email@example.com]</a>
        for feedback, bug reports, or support, we will receive your email address
        and the content of your message. We use this information only to reply to
        you and improve the App. We do not sell or share this correspondence.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 4. ADVERTISING -->
    <section id="advertising">
      <h2>4. Advertising (Google AdMob)</h2>

      <div class="callout callout-ads">
        <strong>This app displays advertisements served by Google AdMob.</strong>
        AdMob is a third-party advertising service that may collect and process
        certain device and usage information in order to serve ads, prevent
        fraud, and measure performance. This section describes that collection
        in detail.
      </div>

      <h3>4.1 What AdMob collects</h3>
      <p>
        When you use SafeHSE, the Google Mobile Ads SDK (part of Google AdMob)
        may automatically collect the following types of data:
      </p>
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Data type</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>IP address</strong></td>
            <td>Used to estimate general (city-level) location for ad targeting and fraud prevention</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Device or other identifiers</strong> (Android Advertising ID, App Set ID)</td>
            <td>Used to serve relevant ads, limit ad repetition, measure ad performance, and prevent fraud</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>User product interactions</strong> (app launches, ad clicks, ad views, in-app actions)</td>
            <td>Used for advertising analytics, attribution, and performance measurement</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Diagnostic information</strong> (app launch time, lag rate, energy usage, SDK performance)</td>
            <td>Used to diagnose crashes, measure SDK performance, and prevent fraud</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Approximate location</strong> (derived from IP address only)</td>
            <td>Used for regional ad targeting and compliance with local advertising laws</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h3>4.2 How AdMob data is used</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>To display advertisements (including personalized ads where you have consented)</li>
        <li>To measure ad performance and improve ad relevance</li>
        <li>To detect and prevent invalid traffic and fraud</li>
        <li>To comply with legal requirements in your region</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>4.3 Data transmission and security</h3>
      <p>
        All data transmitted to Google AdMob is encrypted in transit using
        TLS/HTTPS. AdMob stores data on Google's servers according to
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's own retention and security policies</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>4.4 Personalized vs. non-personalized ads</h3>
      <p>
        Where required by law (for example, in the European Economic Area, the
        United Kingdom, and Switzerland), we will request your consent before
        serving personalized ads through a Google-certified consent flow. If you
        do not consent, you may still see ads, but they will be
        <strong>non-personalized</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        In other regions, including India, ads may be personalized using the
        Android Advertising ID unless you have opted out (see Section 8.3).
      </p>

      <h3>4.5 Your control over advertising data</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Reset your Advertising ID:</strong> On Android, open
          <em>Settings → Google → Ads</em> and tap <em>Reset advertising ID</em>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Delete your Advertising ID:</strong> On Android, open
          <em>Settings → Google → Ads</em> and tap <em>Delete advertising ID</em>
          (Android 12+). This disables personalization based on the Ad ID.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Opt out of personalized ads:</strong> On Android, open
          <em>Settings → Google → Ads</em> and turn on <em>Opt out of Ads Personalization</em>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>4.6 Google's privacy policy</h3>
      <p>
        Google's handling of data collected through AdMob is governed by
        Google's own privacy policies:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Advertising Technologies &amp; Partner Sites</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 5. HOW WE USE -->
    <section id="how-we-use">
      <h2>5. How We Use Information</h2>
      <p>We use the information described above only to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Remember your language, theme, and notification preferences</li>
        <li>Save your study progress, bookmarks, notes, and test results</li>
        <li>Show you your progress and performance summaries</li>
        <li>Send you study reminders if you opt in</li>
        <li>Display advertisements through Google AdMob (as described in Section 4)</li>
        <li>Reply to your support or feedback emails</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do <strong>not</strong> use your information for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Selling your personal data to third parties</li>
        <li>Profiling you beyond the ad personalization performed by Google AdMob</li>
        <li>Any automated decision-making that has a legal or significant effect on you</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 6. DATA SHARING -->
    <section id="data-sharing">
      <h2>6. Data Sharing and Disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        We do <strong>not</strong> sell, rent, or trade your personal information
        with third parties. However, the App does share limited data with the
        following service providers as required to operate:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Google AdMob (advertising):</strong> The Google Mobile Ads SDK
          transmits the data listed in Section 4.1 directly to Google for the
          purpose of serving and measuring ads. This is governed by
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Play (distribution):</strong> Basic installation and
          crash data may be collected by Google Play for app distribution and
          stability, as described in Section 3.4.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may also disclose information in the following limited circumstances:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Legal requirements:</strong> If required by law, court order, or
          government authority, we may disclose information we hold (in practice,
          only the email correspondence you have sent us).
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 7. DATA STORAGE -->
    <section id="data-storage">
      <h2>7. Data Storage and Security</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>All study progress, bookmarks, notes, and test results are stored <strong>only on your device</strong>.</li>
        <li>We do not operate any servers that store your study data or personal data.</li>
        <li>
          Data transmitted by the Google Mobile Ads SDK is encrypted in transit
          (TLS/HTTPS) and handled by Google according to its own security
          policies.
        </li>
        <li>
          If we introduce cloud sync, backup, or user accounts in a future
          version, we will update this policy and ask for your explicit consent
          before uploading any data.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Because your study data lives on your device, its security depends on the
        security of your device (screen lock, encryption, OS updates). We
        recommend keeping your device protected with a screen lock and
        installing operating-system updates.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 8. CHILDREN -->
    <section id="children">
      <h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        SafeHSE is an educational app intended for users aged
        <strong>13 and older</strong> who are studying industrial safety or
        preparing for HSE careers. It is not directed at children under 13.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.
        Ads served through AdMob are configured so that the App is not tagged for
        child-directed treatment. If you believe a child has provided us with
        personal information (for example, by emailing us), please contact us at
        <a href="mailto:[your-email@example.com]">[your-email@example.com]</a>
        and we will delete it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 9. YOUR RIGHTS -->
    <section id="your-rights">
      <h2>9. Your Rights and Choices</h2>

      <h3>9.1 Control over your on-device data</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Access and modify:</strong> View your progress, bookmarks, and notes from within the App.</li>
        <li><strong>Delete local data:</strong> Go to <strong>Settings → Reset All Progress</strong>, or uninstall the App.</li>
        <li><strong>Disable notifications:</strong> Turn off notifications from your device settings or from within the App.</li>
        <li><strong>Change language or theme:</strong> Available any time in Settings without affecting your progress.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>9.2 Control over advertising data</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Reset your Advertising ID</strong> — Android: <em>Settings → Google → Ads → Reset advertising ID</em></li>
        <li><strong>Delete your Advertising ID</strong> — Android 12+: <em>Settings → Google → Ads → Delete advertising ID</em></li>
        <li><strong>Opt out of personalized ads</strong> — Android: <em>Settings → Google → Ads → Opt out of Ads Personalization</em></li>
        <li><strong>Consent (EEA/UK/Switzerland):</strong> You will be asked for consent before personalized ads are shown, and you can change it later from within the App where such a control is provided.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>9.3 Regional rights (GDPR, UK GDPR, DPDP Act)</h3>
      <p>
        If you are located in the European Economic Area (EEA), the United
        Kingdom, or India, you may have additional rights under GDPR, UK GDPR,
        or the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (India).
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          We do not store your study data on our servers — it remains on your
          device under your control.
        </li>
        <li>
          Personal data collected by Google AdMob is controlled by Google. You
          can exercise your rights regarding that data directly through your
          Google Account and Google's privacy tools.
        </li>
        <li>
          For any request you cannot fulfill yourself, email us at
          <a href="mailto:[your-email@example.com]">[your-email@example.com]</a>
          and we will respond within 30 days.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 10. THIRD PARTY -->
    <section id="third-party">
      <h2>10. Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>
        The App currently integrates the following third-party service:
      </p>
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Service</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
            <th>Privacy Policy</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
